From 4419471166fa41ecc00f7c4db90fc1fef5630a1e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Malard <malard@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 12:33:23 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] [VFS][VFSEntry] Read the preformatted-label flag from the
 property's value

A VFS add-on asks for its labels to be shown as given by setting the
item property propmisusepreformatted to "true". After matching the
property by name, the conversion compared the name, not the value, to
"true", so the test could never pass and SetLabelPreformatted(true) has
never run since VFS add-ons were added in db313a1567.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit a868140f9585818aadbedb3a0c58ee752e1fad3c)
---
 xbmc/addons/VFSEntry.cpp | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/xbmc/addons/VFSEntry.cpp b/xbmc/addons/VFSEntry.cpp
index 94e2f08..c2b5432 100644
--- a/xbmc/addons/VFSEntry.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/addons/VFSEntry.cpp
@@ -510,7 +510,7 @@ void VFSDirEntriesToCFileItemList(int num_entries, const VFSDirEntry* entries, C
     {
       if (StringUtils::CompareNoCase(entries[i].properties[j].name, "propmisusepreformatted") == 0)
       {
-        if (StringUtils::CompareNoCase(entries[i].properties[j].name, "true") == 0)
+        if (StringUtils::CompareNoCase(entries[i].properties[j].val, "true") == 0)
           item->SetLabelPreformatted(true);
         else
           item->SetLabelPreformatted(false);
-- 
